WEBVTT

00:00:15.320 --> 00:00:20.760
The following film, The Miracle of Life, is about the process of human reproduction.

00:00:21.840 --> 00:00:24.840
Please use discretion when choosing to view the program.

00:00:31.150 --> 00:00:36.960
Four and a half billion years ago, the young planet Earth was a mass of cosmic dust and particles.

00:00:37.260 --> 00:00:45.800
It was almost completely engulfed by the shallow primordial seas.

00:00:51.270 --> 00:00:54.370
Beautiful winds gathered random molecules from the atmosphere.

00:00:59.040 --> 00:00:59.980
Some were deposited...

00:01:00.000 --> 00:01:15.740
in the seas, winds and currents swept the molecules together. In this ancient ocean,

00:01:16.530 --> 00:01:17.930
the miracle of life began.

00:01:30.090 --> 00:01:34.190
The first organized form of primitive life was a tiny protozoan.

00:01:40.670 --> 00:01:43.390
The protozoa populated the ancient seas.

00:01:43.710 --> 00:01:58.750
The organisms were completely self-sufficient in their seawater world.

00:02:06.560 --> 00:02:11.190
They moved about their aquatic environment, feeding on bacteria and other organisms.

00:02:11.190 --> 00:02:24.120
They were covered with hundreds of tiny whipping hairs called cilia and flagella that made movement possible.

00:02:35.920 --> 00:02:39.560
And these one-celled organisms evolved all life on Earth.

00:02:39.720 --> 00:02:53.540
And the foundation of life, the cell, has endured unchanged since the first tiny organisms swam in the cradle of life, the sea.

00:02:58.190 --> 00:02:59.970
The living being is made up of cells.

00:03:00.500 --> 00:03:02.460
The basic units of life on Earth.

00:03:11.040 --> 00:03:15.340
Cells reproduce themselves by dividing into two identical cells.

00:03:26.270 --> 00:03:28.910
This is a single body cell from a human being.

00:03:30.600 --> 00:03:34.220
And this is the process by which all cells reproduce.

00:03:42.240 --> 00:03:45.670
There are two cells, each exactly like the parent.

00:03:49.920 --> 00:03:54.010
The cell's nucleus is the extraordinary chemical substance DNA.

00:03:57.240 --> 00:03:59.760
The DNA is contained in 46 chromosomes.

00:04:00.220 --> 00:04:09.780
in every cell of the human body each chromosome in turn is made up of thousands of genes discrete

00:04:09.780 --> 00:04:16.880
segments of dna which lie along the chromosome trading even deeper into the structure of the

00:04:16.880 --> 00:04:24.820
chromosome we see the dna molecules themselves dna contains all the genetic information of the cell

00:04:24.820 --> 00:04:29.970
and it is the only living substance capable of reproducing itself exactly.

00:04:31.110 --> 00:04:36.000
Without DNA, duplication, and therefore life itself, is not possible.

00:04:38.630 --> 00:04:42.150
All DNA in all living organisms is chemically identical.

00:04:43.720 --> 00:04:48.560
But its arrangement in genes and chromosomes determines what the cells will become.

00:04:49.640 --> 00:04:52.660
Here, a tiny primitive organism, the protozoan.

